# __PROJECT_NAME__

Standard FPGA project scaffold for **__VENDOR__**. Project-specific device, clocks, resets, interfaces, constraints, and acceptance evidence must be recorded in this repository before implementation or sign-off.

## One-click entry points

- `project/script/run.bat`: invokes the confirmed native build adapter; no argument defaults to a compile/synthesis checkpoint.
- `simulation/script/run.bat`: invokes the confirmed native simulator adapter; no argument defaults to GUI and `batch` supports automation.
- `linter/script/run.bat`: invokes a configured real lint tool or fails closed.

The visible `script/` directories contain only user-facing BAT entry points, `setting.bat`, canonical lists, and confirmed Tcl/DO files. Generated-project desktop runtime does not require Codex-bundled PowerShell. Package installation and Codex-side scaffolding may still use PowerShell internally.

The scaffolded `vendor-build.bat` and `vendor-sim.bat` intentionally fail closed. After the exact device, tool version, project marker, simulator, and vendor libraries are confirmed, replace those placeholders with the validated native Tcl/DO/CLI recipes. A missing tool, library, source, case, or target remains `UNVERIFIED`; it is not silently replaced.

Formal vendor project state, databases, logs, and reports belong under `project/par`. Formal ModelSim/Questa export, local work libraries, logs, and waves belong under `simulation/work`. Codex experiments and review packets belong under `codex_out`. Release candidates are promoted explicitly to `release/output/` after project-defined review.

## Project structure

```text
document/
project/{rtl,sdc,par,script}/
simulation/{tb/case,script,work}/
linter/script/
release/output/
codex_out/
```

Optional `project/ip`, `linter/lint_bb`, and `release/golden` directories are created only when requested by the scaffold command.

These canonical names are fixed for generated projects. Do not create numbered standard directories such as `project2`, `par2`, or `script2`.
